# Analyzer diagnostics

**This script is meant to be read in the editor, not run.** It shows two kinds of
live feedback that RunPad gives while you type C#:

1. A compiler error with a quick fix: `JsonSerializer` is not in scope, so the line is
   underlined as an error. Put the caret on that line and click the lightbulb in the
   gutter to choose `using System.Text.Json;`. RunPad adds the namespace to the
   `namespaces:` list in this file's front matter instead of inserting a `using` line.
2. RunPad analyzer warnings: both `Parse` calls get a constant string that is outside
   the range of the target type, so they always throw `OverflowException`. These
   warnings come from RunPad's own analyzer (diagnostic ID RPAD0258).

Until the quick fix is applied, Run stops with the compiler error. After it is applied,
Run compiles the script and the first `Parse` call throws `OverflowException`.

```csharp run
var settings = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new { Name = "RunPad", Version = 1 });
Console.WriteLine(settings);

var small = byte.Parse("300");
var large = int.Parse("3000000000");
Console.WriteLine($"{small} {large}");
```
